const BRIEF=["Aasha Group started with a casual conversation between two friends in a closed room during COVID, saying 'kuch karte hai yrr' followed by a few phone calls, an Instagram page, and probably more ambition than we had any business having.","What started small grew into a commitment to work on issues that genuinely matter, from the environment and community welfare to mental health, self-care, and social stigma.","Our vision is simple: to turn concern into action, create space for conversations that matter, and keep showing up where change is needed."];
const GAL=[["Food Packet Distribution","2021","Aasha Group’s first initiative, launched during the COVID-19 lockdown, distributing 100+ food packets to individuals and families affected by the crisis."],["Plantation Drive","2021","Organised a plantation initiative with saplings selected according to local environmental conditions. Volunteers continued to care for and monitor the plants beyond the initial activity."],["Ration Kit Distribution","2021","Distributed essential ration kits following the COVID-19 lockdown, with each kit containing provisions intended to support a family of six for approximately one month."],["Carnival of Rising Talent","2021","Organized a non-profit exhibition providing independent artists, sculptors, and creators with a platform to showcase their work directly to audiences, reducing dependence on intermediaries and commissions."],["Blood Donation Camps","2022 and 2024","Organised two-day blood donation camps in collaboration with the Indian Red Cross Society and MY Hospital Blood Bank, bringing together 70+ donors in 2022 and 150+ in 2024."],["Break the Stigma Series","2022","Created an open space to discuss topics including menstrual hygiene, self-awareness, self-defence, domestic violence, and mental health. Interactive activities and anonymous sharing encouraged participants to engage with subjects often surrounded by silence and discomfort."],["One Year Drive","2022","Engaged with children through interactive games, conversations, and recreational activities. The initiative concluded with the distribution of stationery kits and refreshments, creating a day centered around connection, participation, and joy."],["For Your Issues","2024","A one-day mental health initiative featuring counsellor and therapist-led discussions, interactive activities, and group conversations designed to help teenagers understand and express their emotions more openly."],["SUSxHive","2025","A two-day sustainability think tank organised with local urban government bodies of Indore and speakers from UNICEF. The programme combined expert discussions, field visits, workshops, and idea presentations to connect sustainability challenges with practical solutions."]];
